  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n#261 part 3 (parts 1 and 2 shipped in PR #349 and PRs #678/#684): a refused generation now shows the moves the generator had built when it refused, as a **display-only diagnostic ghost**.\r\n\r\n- **Carrier (one channel, part 2's).** `GenError` gets a `Ghosted { msg, at, ghost }` variant (`with_ghost`, `ghost()`, `map_ghost`, `map_msg`, `without_ghost`). It reads exactly like the plain refusal, so no message changes. The new type `machining2d::Ghost` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/ghost.rs`) is bounded at 100 000 moves (it sets `truncated` when capped) and never holds a non-finite move. Its `Debug` prints only its size. `CommandError::MachiningGhost` carries the ghost in world coordinates: a 3+2 tilt maps it through the same `world_path` as a real path. The UI keeps it in `State::feedback_ghost` and reads it only through `State::refusal_ghost()`, which uses the same lifecycle law as part 2's `refusal_focus`.\r\n- **Viewport.** `crates/ui/src/refusal_ghost.rs` draws the ghost dashed in the palette's gouge colour, dimmed (rapids dimmer still), with no chevrons, under part 2's spot cross. The only edit to the large files is one call in `interact::toolpath_lines`.\r\n- **Never a toolpath.** The ghost rides the error only. It is never written to the operation, so nothing caches, simulates, verifies or posts it. It is freed when the refusal retires: on the next command (a regeneration included) or an edit of the draft.\r\n- **Script / MCP.** The `generate` error adds the ghost's move count (\"a partial path of N move(s) was built before the refusal; it is not kept\"). The moves themselves are not included.\r\n\r\n### Generators that carry a ghost\r\n- The ladders' centre-cutting refusal (`approach::refusal` on the finished builder): 2D Pocket / Adaptive / Offset, Contour (rings and open chains), Slot (both kinds), Bore, Circular, and the 3-D ladder (Pocket3D, Multi-Axis Rough).\r\n- The plunge law's after-the-fact audit (`plunge_law::audit*`): the 3-D finish and multiaxis centre-cut guards, Rotary Offset's bar audit, the posed audit (Multi-Axis Rough) and the facer's air-entry fallback. Here the ghost is the whole audited path, shown beside part 2's spot.\r\n\r\n### Generators that carry none (by design, listed in `docs/decisions/261-refusal-ghost.md`)\r\n- Refusals raised before anything is built: parameter doors, drilling, the bore and thread-mill hole doors, region and tool gates.\r\n- Rotary Offset's wrap-space ladder drops its ghost (`without_ghost`). Its moves live in the development, not where the part is.\r\n- Generators that return before `finish()`. Getting a path out of them would mean restructuring them.\r\n\r\n## Pins\r\n- **No toolpath, no post, no sim:** `refusal_ghost::an_op_with_a_ghost_has_no_toolpath_and_the_post_and_the_sim_refuse_it` (app). After a refused generation that carries a ghost: `toolpath_of` is `None`, the status is `Never`, `posting::program_ops` says \"SLT: no toolpath yet\", and `stock_sim::simulate_document` refuses.\r\n- `refusal_ghost::a_refused_slot_hands_back_its_built_moves_in_world`, `a_centre_cutting_tool_generates_the_slot_and_carries_no_ghost`, `the_script_and_mcp_refusal_names_the_ghosts_size_not_its_moves` (app).\r\n- `refusal_ghost_tests::a_refused_generation_draws_its_ghost_and_caches_nothing`, `refusal_ghost_tests::the_ghost_retires_with_the_refusal` (ui lib: the ghost is freed, not only hidden).\r\n- `refusal_ghost::tests::a_ghost_draws_dashed_in_the_dimmed_gouge_colour_and_never_in_a_path_colour`, `a_long_move_is_capped_in_dashes_not_in_length` (ui, path_lines-style structural asserts; no PNG).\r\n- motion: `refusal_ghost::a_ladders_centre_cut_refusal_hands_back_the_moves_it_had_built`, `refusal_ghost::the_plunge_audit_hands_back_the_path_it_judged_beside_its_spot`, `machining2d::gen_error::tests::{a_ghosted_refusal_reads_exactly_like_the_refusal_without_it, the_ghost_rides_the_frame_and_the_sentence_rewrites_keep_it}`, `machining2d::ghost::tests::*` (cap, non-finite drop, frame map).\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` is green: motion suites ok (464 s, includes center_cut_law/owed/posed, entry_approach, ruling, finish3d, multiaxis, rotary_*, refusal_ghost), app suites ok (679 s, includes refusal_ghost, refusal_location, area_controls, center_cut_multiaxis, center_cut_owed, operations, scripting, mcp, posting, stock_sim_document), ui suites ok (112 s, lib includes refusal_focus_tests, refusal_ghost_tests, path_lines::tests, warned_moves). That is 3 steps, 21 min wall, 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n- The on-screen look (dash length, dim level, how readable it is in the light theme) was not hand-checked. The GUI was not launched.\r\n- No snapshot PNG changed, and no golden CL/NC changed: the change adds no output.\r\n\r\nChangelog: A refused generation now draws the moves it had built before refusing as a dashed \"ghost\" in the refusal colour (display only; never cached, simulated or posted), and the script/MCP generate error names its move count (#261)\r\n\r\nEffort: high (no escalation)\r\n\r\nFixes #261: with parts 1 (#349) and 2 (#678, #684) shipped, this covers the issue's whole ask: warned moves are marked, a refusal marks its spot, and a refused generation shows its partial path.\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n",
